// **The pellet an ant carries out of its own tunnel** — tamped ground that
// has been *placed* rather than cut, and the difference between those two
// things is the whole reason this file exists.
//
// `packedsoil` is the wall of a gallery: soil an ant worked *in situ*, with
// the bank still around it. It is `self_supporting` so that a tunnel roof
// cannot fall in, and that is exactly right for a roof — a roof has air
// beneath it by definition and is held by the bank at both ends.
//
// A dumped pellet is the same act on a cell in the open air, and it inherits
// a promise it has not earned: nothing may make it fall. So whatever it was
// resting on can be dug away, slump, or wash out, and the pellet stands there
// for ever. Stack spoil on spoil and the result is a lattice of dirt hanging
// in the sky over the anthill, which the owner has now reported three times
// from three different pictures — 2026-08-31 (*"it looks like there's a lot of
// dirt just floating in the midair"*), and twice in round thirty on cards that
// asked about something else entirely (`Reports/open-bugs-handoff.md` §Z18).
//
// **Four attempts to fix that by asking about the *shape* of the lattice are
// on the record and none of them worked**, which is `CLAUDE.md`'s oldest
// finding about this engine: geometry cannot tell a wall from a heap, because
// a gallery roof and a hanging slab are the same shape. `update.rs`'s crumb
// rule is the survivor of that family and it only reaches a cell touching
// almost nothing — a 2x2 block in mid-air sits at three contacts and stands.
//
// So the difference is stated as **data**, the same remedy `packedsoil.ron`
// itself records: `needs_footing`. A pellet is a wall only while something is
// directly beneath it. Dig out from under your own tailings and the overhang
// comes down, a cell at a time, as loose dirt — which is what a spoil heap
// does and what the player expects when they undermine one.
//
// **What it deliberately is *not*:**
//
// * **Not loose.** Putting the pellet back as tilth was measured on 2026-08-31
//   and it is the difference between a nest and no nest: loose soil set down
//   near a gallery runs along it and closes it, `labnest` roofed void **2/1
//   against 54/58**. Recorded in `Reports/dead-ends.md`. A heap of this still
//   stands as a heap; only the parts with nothing under them come down.
// * **Not a decay path, yet.** `Reports/evolution-lab-soil-design-2026-09-12.md`
//   §3b wants dumped spoil to weather back to `soil` over a session, on
//   `decays_into` plus the two chances, and that is the substrate it needs —
//   the whole reason weathering could not be scoped onto `packedsoil` is that
//   sites are scheduled by *material* at chunk settle, so a gallery lining
//   would weather with the tailings. Left unset here: this file's change is
//   the support rule, and a clock on top of it is that lane's to set from a
//   sweep.
// * **Not a different colour.** Byte-identical to `packedsoil`'s palette on
//   purpose, so the paired card shows the floating ground going away and
//   nothing else. `soilfork mode=fork` tints the two soils apart when the
//   question is which is which.
//
// Every other field is `packedsoil`'s, because every other thing about a
// pellet is true of a wall: it is still ground a root can thread (the same
// `penetration_resistance`, so a species that can cut a lining can cut this),
// it still holds the water the dug cell carried up from depth, and
// `packs_into` means an ant that works a pellet into the side of a tunnel
// through its own mound gets a real wall out of it — which is what stops this
// rule from being "you cannot tunnel through your own spoil".
(
    name: "spoil",
    display: "Spoil",
    kind: Powder,
    density: 1.5,
    friction_angle: 45.0,
    penetration_resistance: 0.95,
    water_capacity: 1000,
    blast_resistance: 0.6,
    slumps_into: "soil",
    // **The wall an ant makes of a pellet it has worked in place.**
    // `line_burrow` reads this on the eight cells around every dig, so a
    // tunnel driven through a heap of tailings has `packedsoil` walls and a
    // `packedsoil` roof, and stands like any other gallery. Without it the
    // roof of that tunnel would be spoil with air beneath it and would come
    // straight back down.
    packs_into: "packedsoil",
    // A pellet re-dug is still a pellet. Without this, hauling spoil twice
    // would launder it into lining-grade ground and the lattice would come
    // back through the second dig.
    spoils_into: "spoil",
    self_supporting: true,
    // **The one field that separates this from `packedsoil`.** See the header,
    // and `update_powder`'s crumb rule for the reading.
    needs_footing: true,
    // `packedsoil`'s own palette, byte for byte -- see the header.
    colors: [
        (48, 38, 32),
        (56, 45, 38),
        (42, 33, 28),
        (62, 50, 42),
        (39, 30, 23),
        (45, 36, 28),
        (33, 25, 19),
        (51, 41, 32),
        (74, 64, 54),
        (84, 73, 61),
        (65, 56, 47),
        (92, 80, 67),
    ],
    base_colors: 4,
)
